pipewire-configurator (2.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The requested latency is no longer written for the PulseAudio bridge,
    where it had no effect; the Streams page explains where to set it.
    Stream settings replace what applications choose themselves, and the
    help texts now say so.
  * Per-program settings for native PipeWire programs (Applications page,
    "PipeWire program"): all Streams settings, saved as stream.rules in
    client.conf.d. They replace the Streams page and the program's choice.
  * Graph settings also apply where PipeWire's own rules change them, for
    example the minimum quantum of 1024 on virtual machines.
  * Bluetooth codec and role lists replace the lists of other configuration
    files instead of being merged with them. mSBC and LC3-SWB can be chosen
    in the codec list, and a warning shows when mSBC is left out of it. The
    LC3 entry is gone: LE Audio is switched with the LE Audio roles.
  * Device pages warn when the device cannot be opened with the chosen
    sample format or rate, and explain a device that disappeared.
  * Sample formats: 24 bit in 32 is S24_32LE, packed 24 bit is S24LE.
    S24_3LE, which PipeWire does not know, is removed from saved settings.
  * Files saved by earlier versions are shown as unsaved changes with an
    explanation; saving rewrites them, the settings stay the same.

 -- Timon <timon2201@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:34:42 +0100

pipewire-configurator (2.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed to Pipewire Configurator: package pipewire-configurator (replaces
    pipewire-configurator-simple), program and desktop file
    pipewire-configurator, repository WhitePeace36/PipewireConfigurator.
  * The drop-in files are now called 60-pipewire-configurator.conf. Files saved
    by 2.0.x (60-simple-configurator.conf) are renamed on the first start, so
    their settings are kept.

 -- Timon <timon2201@gmail.com>  Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:55:00 +0100

pipewire-configurator-simple (2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rework around drop-in files: only the configurator's own files are written.
  * Per-device output and input settings, Bluetooth settings and per-application
    rules (WirePlumber 0.5).
  * Quantum limit is also written to the client configurations.
  * Qt Widgets interface, new icon.

 -- Timon <timon2201@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100

